-- HFGROW_PHASEFIELD (C28): the HFGROW_INJECTION model with the fracture length taken from an in-run phase-field model.
-- HFGROW F1 ... PHASEFIELD 0.002: K_IC = 1 MPa m^0.5, sigma_min = 340 bar, initial half-length 20 m; at the end of every
-- report step a persistent 2-D phase-field model of the fracture plane is loaded with the crack volume
-- V = eta * (water injected) / H (eta = 0.002 for this slow 2 sm3/d injection) and its half-length opens the pieces.
-- Results -> Faults & seismicity -> Fracture growth (phase field): half-length, crack volume, phase-field vs flow pressure.
-- Expected: ~32 m half-length after 88 days (toughness-regime Griffith length ~35 m).
